* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# WHAT GITHUB REPORTS THIS REPOSITORY TO BE.
# Measured with `gh api repos/.../languages` at contract v2.0.0: **Python 116,487 bytes and nothing
# else** — 100% Python for a repository whose substance is 34 language packs, a contract and a set
# of worked examples. Linguist excludes prose by default and treats docs/ and examples/ as
# documentation, so the one directory holding code got the whole bar. That is not a cosmetic
# problem: the language bar is the first thing a reader sees, and it was describing the harness as
# if it were the project.
#
# These overrides make the report match the tree. They do not inflate it: Markdown genuinely is
# most of this repository, and the examples genuinely are Go, Python and TypeScript.
*.md linguist-detectable=true
*.md linguist-documentation=false
examples/** linguist-detectable=true
examples/** linguist-documentation=false
examples/** linguist-vendored=false
languages/**/tools.yaml linguist-detectable=true
atlas.yaml linguist-detectable=true

# The banner is content-addressed and binary; it is not a source file.
docs/assets/** linguist-vendored=true
